982	     * Rolls a registration date forward to a business day. A date that falls on a Saturday, a Sunday
983	     * or a listed {@linkplain #PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS public holiday} is rolled forward one day at a time
984	     * until it reaches the next non-holiday weekday; a date already on a non-holiday weekday is
985	     * returned unchanged. This applies to the effective registration date whether it was supplied in
986	     * the request or defaulted to the server date, and the adjusted value is what gets stored as
987	     * {@code registrationDate} and feeds every value derived from it (such as the member id's
988	     * fiscal-year segment and the daily create-limit's per-day bucket).
989	     *
990	     * @param date the effective registration date, supplied or defaulted
991	     * @return the same date when it is a non-holiday weekday, otherwise the next non-holiday business day
992	     */
993	    private LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
994	        LocalDate adjusted = date;
995	        while (adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY
996	            || adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
997	            || PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(adjusted)) {
998	            adjusted = adjusted.plusDays(1);
999	        }
1000	        return adjusted;
1001	    }
